    description: "Repro: router.ex with `scope \"/api\", AppWeb do resources \"/users\", UserController, only: [:index, :show]; resources \"/posts\", PostController, except: [:delete]; get \"/x\", XController, :x end` -> each resources yields all 7 routes, no PUT, controller `UserController` not `AppWeb.UserController`. The missing scope PATH prefix is WI-kibij (separate). thc's 240 http_route entrypoints (INV-liraj outcome) are affected by both.\n\nFound by the 2026-10-10 docstring-staleness audit (reviewer + default-REJECT verifier, reproduced). Notebook: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_10102026.md."  # 20ab
    fields:  # 20ab
      statement: "Phoenix route markers match what `mix phx.routes` lists for `resources`: 8 actions including PUT /:id -> :update, filtered by only:/except:, with the controller module qualified by the enclosing scope alias."  # 20ab
      root_cause: "elixir.py's resources expansion (~1157-1165) hardcodes 7 routes; the third argument is read only when it is an atom (~1100-1103), so keyword options are ignored; the enclosing `scope ..., AppWeb do` alias is not applied to the controller name."  # 20ab
