- op: discuss  # 8730
  at: '2026-10-11T10:42:21Z'  # 8730
  by: agent  # 8730
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8730
  clock: 3  # 8730
  nonce: '8730'  # 8730
  message: "Fixed in PR #1535 (bb37db9216). Root cause: elixir.py hardcoded a 7-route resources table (no PUT update), read the 3rd arg only as an atom (keyword options dropped), and walked calls with iter_tree, which carries no scope context. Fix: _phoenix_resource_routes mirrors Phoenix.Router.Resource (8 actions, update on PATCH+PUT, only:/except:/singleton:/param:, bare or bracketed keyword list; a non-literal option keeps the full set); _iter_router_calls carries the scope alias (positional or alias:, lexically expanded, nested scopes concatenated, alias: false resets) and every get/post/.../live/resources controller is expanded and then prefixed. Evidence: filed repro (scope \"/api\", AppWeb + resources users only:[:index,:show] + posts except:[:delete] + get /x) -> 'hypergumbo routes <repro> --minimal' prints 'Found 10 API route(s)' incl. [PUT] /posts/:id and [PATCH] /posts/:id, users only GET /users and GET /users/:id; survey meta.controller = AppWeb.UserController / AppWeb.PostController / AppWeb.XController (was 15 routes, unqualified). thc: 377 router markers, fully qualified 2 -> 377, all 373 dispatches_to edges land on the named module (targets unchanged). Scope PATH prefix (/api) is still missing: WI-kibij."  # 8730
